{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "task_family": "incremental_english_modern_japanese_overlay",
  "book_id": "kinkakuji",
  "chunk_id": "kinkakuji-chunk-0810",
  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "\"你听明白了吧？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "You understand now, don't you?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "所谓美就是这样的东西。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "That is what beauty is.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "所以斩猫就像拔掉疼痛的龋齿，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "So cutting down the cat is like pulling out an aching decayed tooth,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "看上去也像把美抠出来，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and it may look as though beauty itself has been gouged out,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "但这是不是最后的解决就不得而知了。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "but whether that is the final solution is impossible to know.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "美的根是不会断绝的，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "The roots of beauty cannot be severed,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "即使猪死了，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and even if the pig dies,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "也许猫的美还没有死呢。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "perhaps the cat's beauty has not died yet.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 9,
      "source_text": "赵州为嘲讽这种解决的简单化，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "In order to mock the simplicity of that kind of solution, Zhaozhou",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 10,
      "source_text": "才把鞋子顶在头上。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "put his sandals on top of his head.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 11,
      "source_text": "也就是说，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "In other words,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 12,
      "source_text": "他知道除了忍受龋齿的痛苦以外，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "he knew that apart from enduring the pain of a decayed tooth,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "kinkakuji-p00810",
      "unit_index": 13,
      "source_text": "别无其他解决的办法。\"",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "there was no other way to resolve it.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
